    "387": {
      "date": "2026-10-26",
      "edition": "Monday 26 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Eligibility hurdle",
          "heading": "Jeremy Ward may need World Rugby permission before playing for France",
          "body": "Jeremy Ward is in Fabien Galthié's 42-man squad for the Nations Championship, but the 30-year-old centre only completes his five-year residency in 2027, so he will train with the group without playing against Fiji, the Springboks or Argentina. The bigger obstacle is his 2016 Junior Springboks appearances, which tied him to South Africa under World Rugby rules. France may need England's route for Benhard Janse van Rensburg: a regulations committee clearance. Ward says: \"I'm not going to say that if I change my nationality, I'll be in the team.\""
        },
        {
