      "edition": "Monday 26 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Obituary",
          "heading": "Former Ireland prop Phil O'Callaghan dies aged 83 after short illness",
          "body": "Phil O'Callaghan, the former Ireland and Munster prop, has died in Dublin at the age of 83 after a short illness. The Dolphin clubman earned 21 caps for Ireland and 34 for Munster across a career that included more than 20 years at Dolphin, and former Ireland captain Terry Kingston led the tributes from his former clubmate. His family, including nephew Mark O'Leary, said they were extremely proud of his achievements with club, province and country. Funeral arrangements have yet to be announced."
        },
