      "edition": "Monday 26 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Red card",
          "heading": "Australia A's David Feliuai sent off in 61-12 rout of USA",
          "body": "Brumbies midfielder David Feliuai was sent off in the 15th minute, yet Australia A still cruised to a 61-12 win over the USA in their opening match in Nashville. Feliuai was first shown yellow for a high shot, then upgraded to red after making contact with an attacker's head, and his side still controlled the game for 80 minutes under Stephen Larkham. Winger Dylan Pietsch scored a double, and Wallabies debutant Harry McLaughlin-Phillips also crossed. The second match is in New Jersey next weekend."
        },
        {
