      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Club exit",
          "heading": "Kwagga Smith's Blue Revs contract terminated by mutual agreement, returns to Bulls",
          "body": "Kwagga Smith's exit from the Shizuoka Blue Revs is confirmed, with the club saying his contract was terminated by mutual agreement. The two-time World Cup winner spent eight seasons in Japan and is heading home to sign a three-year deal with the Bulls. Smith tore his ACL and meniscus in May, ruling him out for the rest of the 2026 season, and medical experts have since cleared him to return to play at the end of December. The club has paid tribute to him as a key player."
        },
