          "heading": "Richie Mo’unga not yet ruled out of Europe tour after calf tear",
          "body": "Richie Mo’unga has not yet been ruled out of the Europe tour, offering the All Blacks a possible boost after the injury list grew following the second Bledisloe Cup Test in Sydney. The flyhalf missed both Bledisloe Tests with a calf tear, and his status remains open even as Leroy Carter’s ankle surgery, Shannon Frizell’s knee and Samisoni Taukei’aho’s calf injury have thinned the squad. The tour opens against Scotland, followed by England and Wales before the finals weekend at Twickenham."
